.TH DCC-CPU-CLI 1 2026-11-22 "Dudes Control Center @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
dcc-cpu-cli \- show and set CPU frequency settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcc-cpu-cli
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcc-cpu-cli
talks to
.BR dcc-cpu-daemon (8)
over
.IR /run/dcc-cpu.sock .
The user must be root or a member of the group
.BR dudes-control-center .
Without options it shows the governor and the frequencies of all cores.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list\-profiles
List the custom CPU profiles with their index.
.TP
.BI \-\-apply\-profile " N"
Apply the custom profile with index
.IR N .
.TP
.BI \-\-governor " name"
Set the governor on all cores, for example
.BR performance ,
.BR schedutil ,
.BR powersave .
Which governors exist depends on the CPU frequency driver.
.TP
.BI \-\-hard\-limit " GHz"
Set the hard frequency limit (for example 3.8).
No core may run above it, whatever profile is active; the
.B dcc-hard-limit-enforcer
timer checks it every 10 seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-hard\-limit\-get
Show the hard frequency limit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error (daemon not reachable, invalid value, refused
command).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dcc-cpu-cli \-\-list\-profiles
.TQ
.B dcc-cpu-cli \-\-apply\-profile 0
Apply the first custom profile.
.TP
.B dcc-cpu-cli \-\-hard\-limit 3.8
Never run faster than 3.8 GHz.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dudes-control-center (7),
.BR dcc-cpu-daemon (8),
.BR dcc-gui (1)
